  "patient": "Yeah, because I just want someone, when I say what I want to say, I just want to know that I'm not just saying it to thin air, it's kind of with someone who really will get it.",
  "therapist": "Sure. Okay, well I guess and thanks for sharing that with me, Alf. And I guess from my perspective, certainly I haven't been through many of the same issues that you have, and you are the expert on your life and your thoughts and feelings at this point in time. I guess for me, perhaps what I bring is just some knowledge about generally how feelings, thoughts, stages of life impact on people. And so I do feel that perhaps we can make some progress together if we combine our two forces, I guess, you with your expertise on you and me with the knowledge of general psychology type stuff. And so what I'm hearing is from you that you don't want it to be like you're speaking in thin air. So would it be helpful as a bit of a process thing if I check in with you, reflect back to you what I'm hearing and give you the opportunity to say, \"No, that's really not quite it\" or \"Yeah, that's spot on\", so you don't feel like it's talking to thin air?",
